# Deposition: the growing wall must not do work on the gas
#
# A depositing surface advances by accretion, not by motion of its material:
# at any instant the patch of atoms a molecule strikes is a stationary piece
# of lattice, and an instant later a new layer of stationary atoms sits in
# front of it.  So the front velocity decides WHEN and WHERE a collision
# happens, but the collision itself is an ordinary stationary-wall event and
# the front velocity must not appear in the reflected velocity.
#
# That is a testable claim.  A wall physically translating at speed s is a
# piston: every rebound adds 2s to the normal velocity and the gas heats at a
# rate set by s.  An accreting wall does not.
#
# The sharp test uses a SPECULAR wall in a closed periodic box.  Specular
# reflection off a stationary plane preserves each particle's speed exactly,
# so the gas temperature cannot change no matter how many times the front
# catches a particle.  Off a moving plane it would change immediately.  Run
# over a range of RATE: with WALL = specular the temperature must be bit
# identical to the RATE = 0 case for every rate at which nothing is buried.
#
# WALL = diffuse is the softer version of the same check, and shows the
# competing effect that makes it softer: a fully accommodating wall is a
# thermostat, and at high growth rates a large fraction of the gas is freshly
# reflected at any instant.  Reflected molecules are drawn flux weighted, so
# they are hotter than the bulk, and the measured temperature drifts up a
# little with growth rate for reasons that have nothing to do with the front
# velocity.  The specular case has no such confounder.

variable            RATE index 0.1
variable            NEVERY index 1
variable            WALL index specular

seed                12345
dimension           2
global              gridcut 0.0 comm/sort yes

boundary            p p p

create_box          0 150 0 150 -0.5 0.5
create_grid         150 150 1
balance_grid        rcb cell

global              nrho 1.0 fnum 0.01

species             air.species N
mixture             air N temp 300.0 vstream 0.0 0.0 0.0

region              inner block 25.5 124.5 25.5 124.5 INF INF
group               inner grid region inner one

fix                 ablate ablate inner ${NEVERY} ${RATE} uniform 1 mode deposit

global              surfs implicit
read_isurf          inner 100 100 1 ../../../examples/ablation/binary.101x101 &
                    180.5 ablate

if "${WALL} == diffuse" then "surf_collide 1 diffuse 300.0 1.0" &
                     else "surf_collide 1 specular"
surf_modify         all collide 1

timestep            0.0001

create_particles    air n 200000

compute             TEMP temp

fix                 check grid/check 1 error

stats               100
stats_style         step np c_TEMP nscoll f_ablate[3] f_ablate[8]

run                 400
